From: Piotr Kubik <piotr.kubik@adtran.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: Do not remove a link of bss[0] when a BSS add fails

setup_interface() gives the driver instance of bss[0] to every BSS.
When hostapd_if_add() fails for a later BSS of an AP MLD, the BSS
keeps that instance with interface_added cleared. The cleanup then
treats the BSS as a link of an added interface and calls
hostapd_if_link_remove() on the driver instance of bss[0]. If bss[0]
has links, that removes a link of another interface and clears the
link context of bss[0], so the next MLD interface event of bss[0]
reaches hostapd_wpa_event() with a NULL context. If bss[0] has no
links, the driver removes the interface and reports
EVENT_MLD_INTERFACE_FREED at once, which reached hostapd_wpa_event()
with a NULL context too. In both cases hostapd crashes.

Clear drv_priv of the BSS when the add fails, as the cleanup does for
an interface that the driver removed.

Fixes: df34c2ced34f ("AP MLD: De-initialize/disable link BSS properly")
---
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -2719,6 +2719,10 @@ int hostapd_setup_bss(struct hostapd_dat
 			wpa_printf(MSG_ERROR, "Failed to add BSS (BSSID="
 				   MACSTR ")", MAC2STR(hapd->own_addr));
 			hapd->interface_added = 0;
+			/* drv_priv is still the driver instance of bss[0], which
+			 * setup_interface() gave to every BSS. The cleanup must
+			 * not remove a link or an interface through it. */
+			hapd->drv_priv = NULL;
 			return -1;
 		}
 
